----------------------------------------- Forms quiz ----------------------------------------------------

1️⃣ How many (non experimental) ways are there to write forms in Angular?

        1

        2   ✅

        3


2️⃣ What classes does Angular offer to handle forms?

        FormControl ✅

        FormValue

        FormGroup   ✅


3️⃣ Which properties are available on these classes?

        dirty   ✅

        empty

        pristine    ✅

        valid   ✅

        touched ✅

        focused 

        value   ✅

        valueChanges    ✅


4️⃣ Angular automatically validates a field if it has validators

        true    ✅

        false (you have to manually watch the field)


5️⃣ How can you do a two-way binding on a field name?

        <input ngModel="name">

        <input [ngModel]="name" (ngModelChange)="name = $event">    ✅

        <input [(ngModel)]="name">  ✅

        <input ([ngModel])="name">


6️⃣ How can you build a form with a field name in a reactive form?

        this.form = formBuilder.group({ name: '' }) ✅

        this.form = new FormGroup({ name: new FormControl() })  ✅

        this.form = formBuilder.control({ name: '' })

        this.form = { name: '' }


7️⃣ How do you use this form in a template?

        <form [formGroup]="form">   ✅

        <form [(formGroup)]="form">

        <form formGroup="form">